msgid "Added to the risk register"
msgstr "Added to the risk register"

msgid "An incident is happening right now (virus, intrusion, data leak)? Do not wait: contact the help desk immediately."
msgstr "An incident is happening right now (virus, intrusion, data leak)? Do not wait: contact the help desk immediately."

msgid "Answer from the person in charge of risks"
msgstr "Answer from the person in charge of risks"

msgid "Answer from the person in charge of risks:"
msgstr "Answer from the person in charge of risks:"

msgid "Choose a risk"
msgstr "Choose a risk"

msgid "Choose the existing risk to link this report to."
msgstr "Choose the existing risk to link this report to."

msgid "Creates a new risk with this title and description, to be completed (owner, likelihood, impact)."
msgstr "Creates a new risk with this title and description, to be completed (owner, likelihood, impact)."

msgid "Decided by %1$s on %2$s"
msgstr "Decided by %1$s on %2$s"

msgid "Decision recorded. The author has been informed."
msgstr "Decision recorded. The author has been informed."

msgid "Describe the situation"
msgstr "Describe the situation"

msgid "Describe what you noticed."
msgstr "Describe what you noticed."

msgid "Examined on %s"
msgstr "Examined on %s"

msgid "Example: the server room door does not lock"
msgstr "Example: the server room door does not lock"

msgid "Existing risk"
msgstr "Existing risk"

msgid "For each new report, add it to the register (a risk is created, to be completed), link it to an existing risk, or reject it with a reason. The author is informed of the decision; the report stays visible on the risk as a trace for the auditor."
msgstr "For each new report, add it to the register (a risk is created, to be completed), link it to an existing risk, or reject it with a reason. The author is informed of the decision; the report stays visible on the risk as a trace for the auditor."

msgid "Give a short title and describe the situation, then send. You only see your own reports here, with the answer of the person in charge of risks once it is examined."
msgstr "Give a short title and describe the situation, then send. You only see your own reports here, with the answer of the person in charge of risks once it is examined."

msgid "Give the reason for the rejection: the author will read it."
msgstr "Give the reason for the rejection: the author will read it."

msgid "Give your report a short title."
msgstr "Give your report a short title."

msgid "How serious does it seem to you?"
msgstr "How serious does it seem to you?"

msgid "I don't know"
msgstr "I don't know"

msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, clause 6.1.2 and control A.6.8"
msgstr "ISO/IEC 27001, clause 6.1.2 and control A.6.8"

msgid "Lets anyone in the organisation point out a risk or a dangerous situation they noticed, without needing access to the risk register."
msgstr "Lets anyone in the organisation point out a risk or a dangerous situation they noticed, without needing access to the risk register."

msgid "Link to an existing risk"
msgstr "Link to an existing risk"

msgid "Linked to an existing risk"
msgstr "Linked to an existing risk"

msgid "Message to the author (optional)"
msgstr "Message to the author (optional)"

msgid "Minor: an annoyance"
msgstr "Minor: an annoyance"

msgid "My risk reports"
msgstr "My risk reports"

msgid "My risk reports page URL"
msgstr "My risk reports page URL"

msgid "No open risk in this entity."
msgstr "No open risk in this entity."

msgid "No report in this list."
msgstr "No report in this list."

msgid "No report is linked to this risk."
msgstr "No report is linked to this risk."

msgid "Not a risk for the organisation, or out of scope. The author reads your reason."
msgstr "Not a risk for the organisation, or out of scope. The author reads your reason."

msgid "Not kept"
msgstr "Not kept"

msgid "Open the reported risks"
msgstr "Open the reported risks"

msgid "Person who reported the risk"
msgstr "Person who reported the risk"

msgid "Read only: triaging requires the right to create and update risks."
msgstr "Read only: triaging requires the right to create and update risks."

msgid "Reason for the rejection"
msgstr "Reason for the rejection"

msgid "Received, waiting to be examined"
msgstr "Received, waiting to be examined"

msgid "Report a risk"
msgstr "Report a risk"

msgid "Reported by"
msgstr "Reported by"

msgid "Reported by %1$s on %2$s (staff report #%3$d)."
msgstr "Reported by %1$s on %2$s (staff report #%3$d)."

msgid "Reports from staff that created this risk or were linked to it."
msgstr "Reports from staff that created this risk or were linked to it."

msgid "Risk created from the report. Complete its owner, likelihood and impact."
msgstr "Risk created from the report. Complete its owner, likelihood and impact."

msgid "Send my report"
msgstr "Send my report"

msgid "Serious: could cause major damage"
msgstr "Serious: could cause major damage"

msgid "Seriousness as felt by the author"
msgstr "Seriousness as felt by the author"

msgid "Significant: could disrupt work or expose information"
msgstr "Significant: could disrupt work or expose information"

msgid "Taken into account: added to the risk register"
msgstr "Taken into account: added to the risk register"

msgid "Taken into account: this risk was already known and is being followed"
msgstr "Taken into account: this risk was already known and is being followed"

msgid "Thank you for your report: every report helps protect the organisation."
msgstr "Thank you for your report: every report helps protect the organisation."

msgid "Thank you, your report has been sent to the person in charge of risks. You will be told what is decided."
msgstr "Thank you, your report has been sent to the person in charge of risks. You will be told what is decided."

msgid "The description is too long."
msgstr "The description is too long."

msgid "The message is too long."
msgstr "The message is too long."

msgid "The risk is already in the register: the report is kept as a trace on it, the risk is not changed."
msgstr "The risk is already in the register: the report is kept as a trace on it, the risk is not changed."

msgid "The title is too long (255 characters at most)."
msgstr "The title is too long (255 characters at most)."

msgid "This report has already been triaged."
msgstr "This report has already been triaged."

msgid "To triage"
msgstr "To triage"

msgid "Triage of the risks reported by staff: each report is examined by a person before anything reaches the risk register."
msgstr "Triage of the risks reported by staff: each report is examined by a person before anything reaches the risk register."

msgid "What did you notice? (short title)"
msgstr "What did you notice? (short title)"

msgid "Where, since when, what could happen, who is concerned. Do not write any password."
msgstr "Where, since when, what could happen, who is concerned. Do not write any password."

msgid "You cannot do this on this report."
msgstr "You cannot do this on this report."

msgid "You have not reported any risk yet."
msgstr "You have not reported any risk yet."

msgid "You noticed something that could harm the organisation or its information: a door left open, a suspicious email, a password written down, a fragile process, a supplier at risk? Describe it below. The person in charge of risks examines every report and tells you what is decided."
msgstr "You noticed something that could harm the organisation or its information: a door left open, a suspicious email, a password written down, a fragile process, a supplier at risk? Describe it below. The person in charge of risks examines every report and tells you what is decided."

msgid "Your risk report has been examined"
msgstr "Your risk report has been examined"

